-- 2026-10-18 (doc 247, step 9): owner-rights functions that only edge functions (through SERVICE-ROLE clients) or the database call,
-- and that the browser never calls, are closed to signed-in users as well as signed-out ones (service role only).
--   * 145 names found by scanning every .rpc() call in supabase/functions and classifying its client: 193 service-role-only names, minus those the app
--     references (as quoted names) in src/. 133 closed, 6 already closed, 6 kept (a policy or caller-run function depends on them).
--   * 16 more found while reviewing the unguarded writers still open to signed-in users (credit_agent_rent_commission, credit_proxy_approval,
--     settle_tenant_rent_from_deposit, collect_due_agent_advance_installment, auto_reject_unmatched_deposits, ...): only mentioned in comments or only
--     called from the database/edge: 16 closed + 1 kept (mature_bonus_by_subject is named in a caller-run function).
--   * NOT closed because an edge function may pass them a signed-in user's client (receiver could not be resolved): log_system_event,
--     record_push_delivery, record_tenant_notification, create_tenant_in_app_notification, compute_daily_stats, landlord_pool_deploy.
-- RESTORE (missed by the name scan): the browser builds these names at run time (`${name}_amclock`, usePaymentBehavior.ts and shortfallRpcNames.ts),
